WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,254
Welcome to the Kony three-six-five Last Man Standing Gameweek One review.

2
00:00:05,204 --> 00:00:10,436
The opening weekend is done, and four players are already six feet deep.

3
00:00:10,436 --> 00:00:18,078
Arsenal were the popular choice, and they delivered: a comfortable three-nil win over Coventry sent eleven players safely through.

4
00:00:18,078 --> 00:00:29,624
Hub showed the casuals what real first-round nerve looks like, backing Ipswich to beat Sunderland two-one and sending Tom Mahon out before he had even had the chance to rekindle his university friendships.

5
00:00:29,624 --> 00:00:33,722
There were more solo picks from people who know ball, too.

6
00:00:33,722 --> 00:00:45,810
Chris Gill got the Seagulls flying, Jordan Padel trusted fellow ginger David Moyes to book his place in the next round, and Alf ended up on the right side of Monday night's bloke-versus-geezer West London derby.

7
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:53,426
Manchester United, meanwhile, were mauled by the Tigers, taking Leicester and newly engaged Tom Davies with them.

8
00:00:53,426 --> 00:00:57,575
He might be going home, but at least it is not an empty house.

9
00:00:57,575 --> 00:01:05,024
Speaking of empty, Cam came in, emptied a full clip of hate on Alf, and then left the building when Forest failed him.

10
00:01:05,024 --> 00:01:12,665
So that is Gameweek One: four down, the survivors move on, and it is time to make another pick or let the wheel decide.

11
00:01:12,665 --> 00:01:15,552
Gameweek Two, here we come.

12
00:01:15,552 --> 00:01:19,959
The deadline is Friday the twenty-eighth of August at seven p.m.

13
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:24,882
British Summer Time, one hour before Crystal Palace against Manchester City.

14
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:29,740
This has been your Kony three-six-five Last Man Standing round review.
